  "id": "discussion/past-sixteen-messages-waiting-for-a-decision-the-oldest-asks-with-no-policy",
  "title": "At most 16 messages wait for a decision: past them, the oldest asks what it asks with no policy, undecided, so a room with no holder alive keeps a bounded queue",
  "rules": [
    "§19.7.5 rule 18",
    "§19.7.5 rule 16"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "RK-19.7.5-164"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: _queue.py KEPT_PENDING = 16, wait_for_decision; test_discussion_dispatch.py test_past_the_messages_that_may_wait_the_oldest_asks_its_candidates. The run's kit installs the discussion and closes: no process that installed it is alive, so nothing is decided. p2 only follows and routes 17 messages: the 17th pushes the first out, which asks every candidate, queued in their order, and 16 stay waiting. Once p2 installs the discussion it takes the lease and decides the 16, the second to the 17th, in order (an empty decision each), before the turns the first asked for.",
